  "about": "Generic laboratory operation vocabulary shared by protocol extraction and equipment capabilities. Nothing here names a protocol, lab or instrument. Hands-on and machine minutes are planning estimates (basis 'planning-estimate') until observed timings replace them. 'scale' says what one occurrence covers: 'batch' = once per batch, 'unit' = once per plate (plate format) or per sample (tube format), 'sample' = once per sample in either format. Consecutive lines of the same batch-scale operation within one step describe one occurrence and are merged. 'loadWhenAutomated' is physical loading that remains when a device performs the operation; it is done when the run is set up. 'reviewWhenAutomated' is result review, done once per operation type at the desk after the run. 'personPerComponent' adds time for each ingredient in a reagent or master-mix table. 'desk' operations (record, calculate, export) count as hands-on time but never need the plate or a trip to the bench.",
